## Original Content
China's top political advisor Wang Huning on Monday urged members of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference (CPPCC) to contribute ideas and efforts to advance the modernization of agriculture and rural areas and urban development.

## Summary
China's top political advisor Wang Huning urged CPPCC members to contribute to modernizing agriculture/rural areas and urban development. This push aims to advance China's overall modernization through targeted development strategies. The focus on both rural and urban sectors suggests a balanced approach to national growth.

## Key Points
- Wang Huning, China's top political advisor, issued a call to action for CPPCC members.
- Focus on modernizing agriculture and rural areas.
- Emphasis on concurrent urban development.


